def normalize_ci(raw):
    """Map an arbitrary `--ci` string onto the closed vocabulary (E3, plan R-B).

    Returns a 2-tuple ``(value, raw_note)``:
      * ``value``    — exactly one of CI_VOCAB.
      * ``raw_note`` — ``None`` unless ``value == "unknown"``, in which case it is the STRIPPED raw
                       string truncated to CI_RAW_NOTE_MAX chars (mr-record puts it in `notes`).

    NEVER raises — including on a non-string input — never dies, never returns anything outside
    CI_VOCAB (A3: `mr-record`'s contract is that a row is never lost; dying on an unmappable
    `--ci` would trade a data-QUALITY problem for a data-LOSS one).

    EVALUATION ORDER, over the WHOLE string, never the head token (the head-token rule in the
    original plan mismapped 21 real rows to `green`, headed by
    'GREEN (CI wf); Nightly RED (mutation job, ...)' — compound verdicts are HOW reds get written):

      0. empty / None / whitespace-only / non-string  -> ("not-recorded", None)
      1. any RED token anywhere                       -> ("red", None)
             \\bred\\b | \\bfail(ed|ure|ing)?\\b | \\bbroken\\b
         Word-bounded is load-bearing, not cosmetic: the real corpus value `rerun-triggered`
         CONTAINS the substring "red" (trigge-RED) and is a PENDING row.
      2. else any HEDGE token anywhere                -> ("unknown", <raw>)
             unverified | expected | assumed | presumed | flake | flaked | flaky |
             cancel | cancelled | canceled | unmerged | stood down | pre-merge | not verified
         An unverified, flaked, cancelled, expected or pre-merge claim is NOT a verdict. 11 real
         corpus rows fall here, and every one of them previously mapped to `green` — e.g.
         'GREEN @ 0421f2c (unverified this tick; stood down before any mutation)'. This rule sits
         ABOVE the compound rule on purpose: several of them name only one verdict family and
         would otherwise map straight to `green`.
      3. else >=2 distinct verdict FAMILIES present   -> ("unknown", <raw>)
      4. else map the single family:
             green   <- green | success | pass | ok
             pending <- pending | in_progress | queued | rerun* | re-run* | retry
             not-applicable <- n/a | not-applicable | no-remote-ci*
         `no-remote-ci*` is matched as a UNIT and consumes the rest of the token, so the real
         corpus value `no-remote-ci-local-gate-green` is `not-applicable` (there is no remote CI on
         the harness repo; the trailing word describes the LOCAL gate) rather than a rule-3
         compound. R-B names this string explicitly as one the new rule handles.
      5. else -> ("unknown", <raw stripped, truncated to CI_RAW_NOTE_MAX>)
    """
    raise NotImplementedError(
        "lp-02 RED: normalize_ci() is not implemented — the closed-vocabulary `--ci` mapper (E3, "
        "plan R-B plus the hedge rule) does not exist yet")


