#     <root>/projects/monster-realm/.claude/worktrees/<project slice>
#     <root>/specs/monster-realm-v2/fixture.spec.md
#
# WHY TWO. Repo A pins the fixed-shape properties that need an exactly-known diff (rename under -M,
# binary record, genuine zero, dirty tree, the walk-up). Repo B exists because repo A's four
# numbers are a transcribable constant: an implementation returning the literal tuple whenever the
# diff is non-empty passed the entire previous battery. B's line counts are derived from
# os.getpid() — deterministic within a run, different across runs — so no expected number in this
# file can be copied into an implementation. B is also PROJECT-routed (so derive must actually call
# worktree_path_for), DELETION-heavy (repo A's prod_lines_deleted is 1 everywhere), and it carries
# five classification rules INSIDE the diff with distinct per-file line counts.
